BT /F1 11 Tf 54 730 Td 15 TL
(Quantitative Portfolio Risk and Asset Pricing Models) Tj T*
(Center for Financial Engineering and Asset Management) Tj T*
(1. The Black-Scholes Option Pricing PDE) Tj T*
(Under geometric Brownian motion for underlying asset price S, the European call price C satisfies:) Tj T*
(dC/dt + \(1/2\) * sigma^2 * S^2 * \(d^2C / dS^2\) + r * S * \(dC/dS\) - r * C = 0) Tj T*
(where sigma is implied volatility and r is the risk-free continuously compounded interest rate.) Tj T*
(2. Modern Portfolio Theory and Sharpe Ratio) Tj T*
(The Sharpe ratio S_p measures excess return per unit of portfolio standard deviation:) Tj T*
(Sharpe Ratio = \(R_p - R_f\) / sigma_p) Tj T*
(Table 1: Asset class performance metrics across a 10-year investment horizon.) Tj T*
(Asset Class     | Annual Return | Annual Volatility | Sharpe Ratio) Tj T*
(US Large Cap    | 12.4%         | 15.2%             | 0.68) Tj T*
(Emerging Mkts   | 8.1%          | 22.4%             | 0.27) Tj T*
(US Treasuries   | 3.2%          | 4.1%              | 0.29) Tj T*
(Commodities     | 5.8%          | 18.6%             | 0.20) Tj T*
(Figure 1 \(Page 1\): The Efficient Frontier curve with capital allocation line tangent at the optimal tangency portfolio.) Tj T*
